# Round tierfam2: Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B UD-Q4_K_XL's routed experts on the card, the RTX 3090 alone. The
# change and the base are lightning-card32-a6000.card's: before this tree the latent MoE body's card arm ran IQ2_XXS
# alone, so the plan left all 2,944 experts on the host; this tree runs the 32-value stacks on the card.
# Base [derived, unmeasured on the 3090]: the A6000's 89.2 tok/s (11.2 ms) is host DRAM 7.5..11.2 ms in series with
# the trunk; the 3090's trunk is the A6000's 2.5..3.7 ms at 936/768 GB/s = 2.05..3.0 ms, so 9.6..14.2 ms: 70..104.
# Room [derived]: 24,576 MiB less 400 driver and 64 scratch = 25.3 GB; less the trunk 2.3 GB (25.5 GB file less 23.2 GB
# of experts), K/V and mamba state at 4,160 positions 0.05..0.1 GB, the pass reserve and leg buffers 0.5..1.9 GB:
# 21.0..22.4 GB of experts at 7.9 MB = 2,650..2,830 of 2,944 on the card, spread a layer at a time (placement.rs
# `spread`): 115..123 of 128 a layer, 110..290 on the host (4..10 % of the picks under even routing).
# Resource timeline, one token at D = 512, 3090 (a layer's card share and its host share run side by side; the next
# layer waits for the join):
#   card SM: trunk 2.05..3.0 ms + the card's 90..96 % of 1.09 GB through the relu² form at 550..850 GB/s (250 W cap)
#            = 1.2..1.9 ms, 52..83 us a layer
#   host DRAM: 44..110 MB a token, 2..5 MB a layer at ~100 GB/s = 20..50 us a layer: under the card's share (worth 0)
#            except a layer whose picks land 2+ on hosted experts: 0..0.4 ms a token
#   join: go, wait, the tier rows and the sum, 20..60 us a layer x 23 = 0.5..1.4 ms (the placed leg's hand-off; PCIe
#            carries 6 rows of 2,688 floats a layer, 1.5 MB a token, < 0.1 ms)
#   => 3.75..6.7 ms: 149..267 tok/s. NVMe 0.
# Sitting (on the lead's go, after gate-gpu-nemotron-h-moe-card32 is green), one lease, base and this tree:
#   BLOOMERY_MODEL=nemotron_h_moe BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/lightning-card32-3090.card
#     BLOOMERY_TIMING_GPU=<the 3090's id, tools/ref/cards.sh GPU_3090> BLOOMERY_REF_MODEL=<the Lightning file>'
#     just depth-serve <base tree>:512 <this tree>:512
#   (the base tree holds its own bloomery-serve build; depth-serve rotates the two arms over BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4)
kind: baseline
question: what does the nemotron seat decode on Nemotron 3.5 Lightning UD-Q4_K_XL at depth 512 on the RTX 3090 alone
  once the card holds most of its routed experts and the host the rest?
term: tg tok/s @ n=1, D = 512, bloomery-serve --model nemotron (place unset -> a, DEPTH_SERVE_CTX 4160), RTX 3090 alone
  at its 250 W cap, depth-serve rows (timings.predicted_per_second over 127 steps)
unit: tok/s
predict: 149..267
condition: depth-serve in its own lease with the 3090 the timing card, one fresh server a row, base and this tree in
  the same lease; this tree's `plan` record holds 2,650..2,830 experts on the card, else the room term is re-derived
  before the row is read; the base row reads 70..104 tok/s, else the trunk term is re-derived first; the witness shows
  no Xid before or after and no other model load
reason: the user asked that every supported model gain from the placement work; the 3090 is the lead's public basis
  and the card that splits Lightning between the card and the host, so this row prices the placed leg's join
decide-in: write the row beside the base's in docs/models.md's Lightning row and the README's 3090 table, with its
  lease and witness
decide-below: read the join term first: nsys on the step graph, the wait per layer against 20..60 us; a longer wait
  is the host share's (its picks per layer, BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS), and the next round is the plan's per-layer split
decide-above: the join is shorter than 20 us a layer or the trunk than 2.05 ms; re-derive both before the A6000 row
  is compared with this one
